     I haven't looked at that patch, and don't actually know--or
particularly care, for that matter--how nethack's tty port deals
with color issues.  But I do recall that when the current color
implementation replaced the prior one (in 3.1.0, I think), there
was a problem when displaying into a DECterm window on the VAX
workstation I was using at the time.  The background color of
the terminal window was not the same as any of the 8 colors you
could select for either background or foreground, and initially
nethack was attempting to explicitly specify background if it
needed to redraw part of an unmapped area.  So the screen
background could be either or two colors depending on how it got
drawn.  The code was changed to do such areas differently, so
that it was always shown as plain background and not explicitly
any particular color.  It sounds as if the patch to your patch
might possibly break that, but the explanation given sounds as
if your patch broke that and somebody tried to fix it.

     I doubt if this is particularly helpful to you, and I don't
have access to that old environment to attempt any testing, but
maybe it'll give a useful hint.  DECterm used black text on an
off-white background by default (although like VT100 and such
there was a setting to reverse those).


